# Summer Sports Games (PPSA03416): cross the logos and the mode selector into the first athletics
# event. Seconds are measured from the first pad poll. These are exactly the Cross anchors recorded
# in issue #1597; no directional input is needed. They are bare time points, so each press holds
# PROSPER_PAD_HOLD (default 300ms, hle_pad.cpp:105).
#
# Observed on a Linux hardware-Vulkan boot through tools/snapshot at PROSPER_RENDER_SCALE=4. This
# title renders at 3840x2160, so scale 4 gives 960x540 frames, not the 480x270 the 1080p titles
# produce -- the guard's dims are 960x540 for that reason. Sampling once per second: black and boot
# logos to 19s, the mode selector and event menus 21-47s, a black load at 48s, then the javelin
# throw event from 49.1s: full stadium, animated crowd, athlete run-up, ATTEMPT 1/3 counter, SPEED
# power meter and the throw reticle.
#
# The run then alternates between live attempts and result overlays, and the last Cross press at
# 115s leaves the game on a static JAVELIN THROW standings screen, which appears at 144s and is
# settled from 150s to the end of the profiled 209s capture. That standings screen is the most
# metrically stable part of the whole run -- all 60 samples from 150s onward measure 48,201-48,489
# colours at 1.0000 coverage, SSIM 1.000 against itself -- so a window chosen by stability alone
# lands on it. It is not gameplay. The guard therefore samples 55-80s, inside the first live attempt,
# which was confirmed by opening the frames.
#
# The right edge was pulled in from 85s after measurement. The end-of-attempt FOUL!/POOR banner at
# 85.2-86.2s is drawn over the same stadium but is not the same visual state: it scored 0.7313 and
# 0.6948 against the reference set built from the original 55-85s window, and scores at most 0.6558
# against the adopted 55-80s references -- below the 0.85 floor either way -- and it carries
# 96,000-102,000 colours against the attempt's 57,000-68,000. With 85s as the edge it drifted in and
# out between runs, eating match margin and swinging the window's richest frame by 1.5x.
#
# Coverage is 1.0000 for every frame of this title, gameplay and menus alike, so non-black coverage
# carries no discrimination here and scene identity rests on SSIM.
